.TH FLTUBE 1 "21 October 2026" "FLTube XR 2.2.0" "de-xr User Commands"
.SH NAME
fltube \- FLTK YouTube browser with DomeD stereoscopic playback
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fltube
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
FLTube searches YouTube with yt-dlp and displays results in a native FLTK
window. Enter a search term or video URL in the application's input field;
there is no positional command-line URL option.
.PP
This fork integrates with DomeD's universal menu and live appearance settings.
It uses mpvr as its default video player. The original webpage URL is passed
to mpvr's yt-dlp hook, retaining the player's audio, seeking and stream handling.
A different player can be configured in fltube.conf.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config= /absolute/path/fltube.conf
Use an existing configuration file instead of the normal configuration search.
The equals sign is required; a separate following argument is not supported.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable verbose diagnostic logging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.SH STEREOSCOPIC PLAYBACK
Choose a layout in the
.B XR video
menu before opening a video: Automatic, Full SBS, Half SBS, Full top-bottom,
Half top-bottom, or Mono. The choice persists between launches.
Automatic selection uses source metadata and explicit packing markers;
ambiguous uploads need a manual choice.
.PP
Full layouts retain each eye's normal dimensions. Half layouts squeeze the
packing axis. Configure
.B \-\-swap-eyes
in STREAM_PLAYER_PARAMS when source eyes are reversed.
.PP
An active DomeD XR session uses mpvr's stereo surface; otherwise playback uses
the desktop. This handles existing flat stereoscopic material, not depth
synthesis or spherical VR180/360 projection. A matching mpvr installation with
top-bottom support is required for those layouts.
.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+L focuses the search/URL field. Ctrl+Q quits.
Other FLTube shortcuts remain configurable in its configuration.
The launched player retains its own playback shortcuts.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration precedence is an explicit
.BR \-\-config= FILE,
then $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fltube/fltube.conf, then
.I PREFIX/etc/fltube/fltube.conf
where PREFIX is the build's installation prefix (normally /usr/local).
An unset XDG_CONFIG_HOME falls back to $HOME/.config.
.PP
STREAM_PLAYER_PATH selects the external player; the default is mpvr.
STREAM_PLAYER_PARAMS supplies player arguments, and
STREAM_PLAYER_EXTRA_PARAMS_FOR_LIVE supplies additional live-stream arguments.
YTDLP_PATH selects a custom yt-dlp executable.
XR_VIDEO_LAYOUT stores the layout selection (0 through 5 in menu order).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fltube/app.conf
Persisted application settings; defaults under $HOME/.config.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/fltube/userdata.txt
Saved user data; defaults under $HOME/.local/share.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/fltube/
Default cache location; defaults under $HOME/.cache.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dome/appearance.json
DomeD appearance settings followed live in Dome sessions. Local color overrides
are disabled there; other desktops retain FLTube's themes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DE_XR_GL_TRACE
Set to 1 to report the selected shared FLTK OpenGL widget renderer.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fltube
fltube --config=/home/user/.config/fltube/testing.conf
fltube --version
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR yt-dlp (1)
.PP
